The '''Concepción–Merced high speed rail line''', marketed as '''''Mercepción''''', is a {{convert|157.07|km|adj=on}} {{W|standard gauge}} {{W|railway line}} that was inaugurated on 22 March 1992. Designed for speeds up to {{convert|360|km/h|mph|0|abbr=on}}, it connects the cities of [[Concepción]] and [[Merced]] (the ''[[Mercepción]]'' metropolis) in 43 minutes.

Trains are operated by the national [[Baliscan Railways Group]] under the [[AVB]] service. 

